# Lower Tail — resting order ops

When duplicate dual rests exist at the same price (e.g. after a mistaken re-place):

1. **Keep the older orders.** They have better queue position.
2. **Cancel the newer ones.** Never cancel the older pair to “clean up.”
3. **No mid-cycle live recovery place** in `lower_tail_agent` — restart during an open cycle skips that cycle.

See `docs/LOWER_TAIL_STRATEGY.md` §5.3 (Queue position).
